BIOSCIENCE WRITERS (BSW) WILL PROVIDE WRITERS/EDITORS TO SUPPORT THE DEVELOPMENT OF CLINICIAN SUMMARIES USING THE METHODS AND PROTOCOLS DEVELOPED BY THE EISENBERG CENTER.  
BSW WILL SERVE AS PART OF THE TRANSLATION TEAM BY CONTRIBUTING TO THE PREPARATION OF, AND WRITING AND EDITING OF, UP TO 10 CLINICIAN SUMMARIES, PROVIDING BETWEEN 60 AND 85 HOURS OF SERVICES FOR OUR COMPONENTS OF THE WORK ON EACH TOPIC AT $100 PER HOUR, TOTALING $85,000 IN DIRECT LABOR COSTS PER YEAR. 
BSW COSTS ALSO INCLUDE A FIXED FEE OF $1,500 PER TOPIC ($15,000 FOR 10 TOPICS ANNUALLY) FOR A TOTAL OF $100,000 PER YEAR FOR UP TO 5 YEARS.  
TASKS THAT BSW WILL ASSIST UNDER EISENBERG CENTER GUIDANCE AND PROTOCOLS INCLUDE ONE OR MORE OF THE FOLLOWING:  
1) PRE-REVIEWING EPC DRAFTS USING THE EISENBERG CENTER CHECKLIST; 
2) REVIEWING AND SUPPLEMENTING (AS NEEDED) FORMATIVE FINDINGS; 
3) PREPARING PROJECT PLANS SPECIFIC TO CLINICIAN TARGET AUDIENCE(S), AND CONTRIBUTING TO DRAFTING THE KEY MESSAGE DOCUMENTS; 
4) PREPARING, IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE MEDICAL CONTENT EXPERT (MCE) AND THE EISENBERG CENTER DIRECTOR OR HIS DESIGNEE, DRAFT CLINICIAN SUMMARIES; 
5) CONTRIBUTING TO PREPARATION OF TESTING PROTOCOLS; 
6) PARTICIPATING IN ANALYZING TESTING RESULTS; 
7) MODIFYING SUMMARIES AS A RESULT OF TESTING AND REVIEWS BY EXPERTS, EXTERNAL ORGANIZATIONS, AND AHRQ; AND 
8) PREPARING THE DISPOSITION REPORT AND THE CONTENT PROOF FOR FINAL INTERNAL EISENBERG CENTER REVIEW FOR SUBMISSION TO AHRQ.

